_014DYSJQHC8M2QyHR9zNAkvT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. Opening the PR now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BCLD5gQ8vK8My2aeVToy2q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch `rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP` \u2192 `rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (and the import accordingly).\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n\nNote: This changes rounding behavior for exact half-cent amounts where the preceding digit is even (they now round down instead of up). This matches the FIN-212 spec.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.94}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the pull request is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said it used banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually rounded half-cents up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). So `2.665` became `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`, and the test failed.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit (`08d3cd5986`).\n- **Pull request:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) against `main`. The description notes that exact half-cent amounts after an even digit now round down instead of up, which is what FIN-212 requires.\n\nI didn't merge it. Merging into `main` needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}